  1) Shift key: Learn when and where to use it.
  2) Return key: Ditto.


  ROT13.  Each alphabetic character is shifted 13 letters:

   abcdefghijklm
   nopqrstuvwxyz

    Note:  'a' goes to 'n' means 'n' goes to 'a', every time.  To
decrypt, just repeat the ROT13.

    Remember a few key pairs and you can almost read it directly:

     "They say that", e.g. goes to "Gurl fnl gung"


  Most newsreaders have the ability to encrypt/decrypt.  Not
surprising, since encryption is the same action as decrypting.
